<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tirana</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tirana is the capital and largest city of Albania, in the centre of the country. Traditionally founded as a town by the Ottoman notable Sulejman Pasha in 1614, it was chosen as the capital by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-lushnje">Congress of Lushnjë</a> in 1920. It grew under Zog, Italian rule and the communist regime of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enver-hoxha">Enver Hoxha</a>, and since 1991 it has become the country's economic and cultural centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tirana.jpg" alt="Tirana" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photo: Chris Walts · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Skanderbeg_square_tirana_2016.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
